Scope of this file

This file covers only original code authored by SG-WorkStation and placed in
the PCL.SGW/ directory of the PCL-CE-SGW repository. Every other part of that
repository keeps its own license.

A file in PCL.SGW/ that copies from, or is derived from, code outside this
directory stays under the license of its source directory (Apache-2.0, or the
custom terms in 'Plain Craft Launcher 2/LICENCE'), and must keep its original
copyright and license notices plus a prominent notice stating that it was
changed. Copying Apache-2.0 code into this directory does not relicense it as
MIT.

The opposite direction is fine: code from this directory may be copied into
one of the Apache-2.0 directories of the repository, and the copy that then
lives there is distributed under Apache-2.0. It simply stops carrying this
grant at that point.

Code from 'SGW.Tools/' may not be copied into this directory: that directory
is under CC BY-NC-SA 4.0, whose ShareAlike condition would require the
resulting file to be shared under CC BY-NC-SA 4.0, which the MIT grant here
cannot cover.

The repository root LICENSE holds the complete path-to-license map. Shipping a
build that includes this directory still requires compliance with Apache
License 2.0 (including the notices in 'PCL.Core/NOTICE') and, where the build
includes the application directory, with the custom terms in
'Plain Craft Launcher 2/LICENCE'.

Suggested header for new source files in this directory:

    // SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT
    // Copyright (c) 2026 SG-WorkStation
